this is evan langer reading for writer  steve watts  ratchet and clank rift apart is only one  month away from release but before that  we received a lengthy final look at the  game and in this video we'll be  discussing our hands-off impressions  with brand new gameplay  if you like this video and want to see  more ratchet and clank rift-to-part  coverage  including our review then consider  subscribing to gamespot when ratchet and  clank rift apart begins  the pair are already famous celebrated  heroes confident in their abilities even  as they're cast  a bit awkwardly into the spotlight it's  a feeling that may be familiar to their  creators insomniac games  the studio has been steadily making a  reputation as a rock-solid developer  with a firm grasp on playstation  technology  but the mega success of 2018's  spider-man and its follow-up miles  morales give its profile an overdue  boost  now as a headliner studio for the new  playstation 5 the developer is  confidently displaying its tech prowess  while managing high expectations  after ratchet and clank are pulled into  a riff by returning villain dr nefarius  they find themselves in an alternate  dimension where the mastermind has been  dubbed emperor nefarious  separated from ratchet in this new realm  clank eventually meets rivet an  alternate universe version of his best  pal who sports blue fur and a cybernetic  arm  developer insomniac game said it  considered making nefarious alternate  dimension and nemesis story a dark  mirror that reflects the inverse of  everything we know  instead creative director marcus smith  said the studio settled on the alternate  dimension showing characters true selves  but altered by the circumstances of  their surroundings  so as a result rivet is naturally heroic  but a little impulsive like ratchet  whereas ratchet has celebrated his  victories and grown up a bit  rivet's impulsivity has helped keep her  alive in the oppressive totalitarian  regime  insomniac told us it wanted rivet to be  a loner but being alone has made her a  little awkward not cynical or  mean-spirited  in the small snippets we've seen so far  that comes through in the performance of  jennifer hale most known for a very  different energy in her confident  portrayal of mass effect's female  version of commander shepard  i don't know about your dimension but  out here things never go according to  plan  improvisation is a skill you learn very  fast  i also have a talent for improvisation  well i can't wait to see you in action  [Music]  the demonstration showed two versions of  the returning setting of megalopolis  from ratchet and clank going commando  initially we see it with the ticker tape  celebration of the titular heroes  swarming with crowds and particle  effects all of which serve as a tutorial  the bright and sunny setting is then  replaced by its doppelganger nevarius  city which is cast at night with  saturated neon lights and traffic  constantly buzzing around its exterior  the ratchet and clank series has handled  cities before but this time it looks  like it could be an actual thriving city  the team said it took a page from  spider-man to have cityscape content  streaming all around you at all times  for a sense of constant bustling  activity  though it isn't an open world game  structure it feels expansive  you're dwarfed by massive art deco  buildings and at the street level  constant movement and small details help  to push the idea that the same is  happening throughout the massive urban  landscape  while some worlds are their own static  environment other planets will show off  the conflict of dimensions and flux  these sync planets will let you explore  a world caught between both realms  by constantly swapping between their  varied states and a snap the bulk of a  ratcheting clank game isn't spent  gawking at the environments  but rather causing havoc inside of them  on that front rift-apart looks familiar  if gorgeous  i should have known scuttling you fools  would be too easy  [Applause]  were you saying something here i stopped  list  [Music]  the thing you'll never have to find out  ratchet and clank gameplay has already  been fine-tuned over more than a dozen  games and there's not much reason for  insomniac to reinvent the wheel  what we see instead are refinements and  new toys to tinker with blending the  studio's eye for varied platforming  challenges with its fine sense of weapon  design  that's where you get elements like the  topiary sprinkler a glove with a green  thumb  that turns your enemies into shrubs  inspired by the greenery art at  disneyland  insomniac said it wanted to introduce a  freezing mechanic without just another  freeze ray and the result is more cheeky  and comical  a ricochet gun based on pinball complete  with a round and silvery projectile  rewards pinpoint timing as you bounce it  repeatedly off the heads of unsuspecting  foes  the void repulsor combines a shield with  a shotgun like short range burst  and the negatron collider is said to  exemplify the mechanical implications of  the new dual sense controller  insomniac noted that the previous charge  mechanics needed to rely on a separate  input or releasing the trigger to fire  while the dual sense lets you charge and  then pull through the adaptive trigger's  resistance to let it rip  what's striking is how the fidelity of  the visual design helps create player  feedback for the weapons  we've heard about the enforcer in other  previews and how it makes use of the  dual sense controller by firing one  barrel with a partial squeeze  and then both if you click past the  resistance but on top of that you can  actually see this reflected on the  weapon itself  without glancing at the weapon hud two  indicator lights on the back of the gun  show when it's empty  partially full or ready for a full  two-barrel blast the over-the-top size  of the weapon makes this small touch  legible at a glance  that same level of care and attention to  detail seems to reflect in the  platforming segment  which transitions seamlessly with quick  cinematic flourishes one major action  set piece  as riven and clank escape from a  rampaging robot blends rail jumping  wall running and the new riff pulling  mechanic into an array of frenetic  action that may seem dizzying if it  weren't so imminently readable in the  heat of the action  rift-apart also adds more traversal  tools to make you more nimble like a  phantom dash that has you phase out of  reality for a short time for a side  strafe maneuver unaffected by gravity or  enemy attacks and even within that  action set piece  rift apart found time to insert little  moments of humor and heart  have any of you seen a little grey robot  anywhere green eyes  red antenna very charming all of this  happens within the snappy  moment-to-moment gameplay  rather than pausing to watch some story  happen and when cut scenes do occur  they're fun to watch and usually pan  right into a moment of gameplay  [Music]  can't anyone print instruction manuals  anymore it's the trick insomniac pulled  with the opening of 2018 spider-man  transitioning straight from a cutscene  to swinging through manhattan so  seamlessly you may not have even noticed  that cutscene was over  that filmic quality is mostly visible in  the characters themselves  if the world has gotten a significant  upgrade to take advantage of the ps5  it doesn't come at the cost of ratchet  clank or rivet in the case of the two  organic creatures  their faces are stretchy and expressive  like an animated film and their fur is  beautifully detailed  you can actually see the direction their  fur is brushed on various parts of their  faces and arms  clank is built to look like he was made  of actual metal materials with a visible  difference between shiny reflective  steel  and coarse brushed nickel his eyes look  like dappled led arrays  and being a metallic companion you could  see raytrace reflections on his face and  body  insomniac recently boasted that it will  have a ton of accessibility options as  well  though we didn't see all of them in  action we did hear about one handy tool  a global time slow that could be mapped  to a shortcut on the d-pad  letting you slow the world if you needed  to get past any dexterity challenges the  studio says it is possible to complete  all the trophies with the accessibility  options turned  on insomniac doesn't seem to be  reinventing ratchet and clank for rift  apart  the series has been so finely tuned and  refined over the years that it's clear  insomniac knows exactly what it is  the bells and whistles here seem to be  variations on its framework so it will  probably feel very mechanically familiar  when the game finally releases on june  11th  but like comfort food at a five-star  restaurant the taste is familiar and  cozy and the presentation  has never looked better  [Music]  don't listen to him if you're broken so  am i and i think we're pretty awesome  thanks for watching if you like this  video then consider clicking the like  button and let us know in the comments  what future rift apart videos you'd like  to see  for all things ratchet and clank stay  tuned to gamespot  [Music]  you

